Yes, it looks like disk "dra0" is having a problem.  This is more than
likely a disk that is behind an on-board RAID controller (i.e. "swxcr"
controller).  If you load "swxcrmgr" from the SRM (>>>) or from a
floppy, you should be able to see if this disk is failing/has failed.
I'm not that familiar with "swxcrmgr" but you should be able to google
something on it.

Hope this helps,

--John Lanier



