that's only going to get you some info like attributes or param/env 
settings. it's not a good synopsis like prtconf.

take a look at sys_check; it generates an html file (based on args for 
specific details) which will generate a lot MORE info/output than prtconf 
yields.. but it takes a bit to collect all the info and it can impact a 
smaller/busy system so perhaps run it at an off-peak time. check out the 
sys_check manpage.

hp also updates it semi-frequently; check 
http://h30097.www3.hp.com/sys_check/ and see if its worthwhile to upgrade 
before running it.

