> the size of /usr, and whats the easiest way to do it?
> 
> I'm hunting through AdvFS resources on the web, but cant  spot an easy
> way out similar to chfs on aix..  Is there an easy way out, or do I
> need to be adding volumes or dump/create new fs/restore etc.. ?

maybe, maybe not.

If you have the advanced AdvFS license, and another partition, 
then you may be able to use:

    addvol /dev/device domain_name

This can be done on-line.

If if this works, you can also use

    addvol /dev/device2 domain_name
    rmvol  /dev/device1 domain_name

as a way to migrate any given domain to a different set of storage 
devices on-line.

All of this depends on whether you have the license that allows 
you to use more than one volume in a domain.  If you can, then a 
domain can be huge.

                                        Bob Harris


